WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:01.801 align:start size:94% position:6%
-How are you, John?
-Hi, Seth.

00:00:01.801 --> 00:00:05.505 align:start size:94% position:6%
This is my little friend, Seth
and he wanted to meet you.

00:00:05.505 --> 00:00:07.140 align:start size:94% position:6%
I hope that's all right.
-Oh, my goodness.

00:00:07.140 --> 00:00:08.641 line:92%
And what a delight to meet him

00:00:08.641 --> 00:00:11.011 align:start size:94% position:6%
-What did you call me,
a comedy legend?

00:00:11.011 --> 00:00:12.846 line:92%
-I called you a comedy legend.

00:00:12.846 --> 00:00:15.949 size:88% position:44%
-No, I've been promoted.
I'm a comedy icon now.

00:00:15.949 --> 00:00:18.351 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, my goodness.
When did that happen?

00:00:18.351 --> 00:00:19.386 line:92%
-It happened last Friday,

00:00:19.386 --> 00:00:22.155 align:start size:94% position:6%
which is why everybody doesn't
know about it yet.

00:00:22.155 --> 00:00:23.223 align:start size:94% position:6%
But I am an icon.
-That's fantastic.

00:00:23.223 --> 00:00:24.858 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, I'm assuming
that's like one of those thing

00:00:24.858 --> 00:00:26.326 align:start size:94% position:6%
where the Queen knights yo
and there's

00:00:26.326 --> 00:00:28.461 align:start size:94% position:6%
different orders of merit,
right?

00:00:28.461 --> 00:00:29.629 size:81% position:41% line:92%
-Well, it's not quite.

00:00:29.629 --> 00:00:37.037
It is a small legislative
occasion in Parliament

00:00:37.037 --> 00:00:38.104 size:81% position:41% line:92%
when you get promoted.

00:00:38.104 --> 00:00:41.041 align:start size:94% position:6%
The next stage for me is
national institution.

00:00:41.041 --> 00:00:44.878
What do you, Seth? Are you
an icon or a legend, perhaps

00:00:44.878 --> 00:00:48.214 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I think I -- you know,
I know I was an "up-and-comer"

00:00:48.214 --> 00:00:50.183 align:start size:94% position:6%
for a long time.
-[ Laughs ]

00:00:50.183 --> 00:00:54.654 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And now, I think the last
I've heard, I'm "established."

00:00:54.654 --> 00:00:55.989 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Ah, very good.

00:00:55.989 --> 00:00:57.457 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, it's not
a bad place to be.

00:00:57.457 --> 00:00:58.591 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Now, Seth, you're very
important.

00:00:58.591 --> 00:01:00.693 align:start size:94% position:6%
Seth, you're
very important to me.

00:01:00.693 --> 00:01:01.928 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, it's a --
you know it --

00:01:01.928 --> 00:01:03.496 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Because you're
the first writer...

00:01:03.496 --> 00:01:05.865 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, thank you.
-...I've spoken to

00:01:05.865 --> 00:01:07.067 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
about the book.

00:01:07.067 --> 00:01:09.135 size:84% position:42%
Because you were, what,
you were head writer

00:01:09.135 --> 00:01:11.471 align:start size:94% position:6%
on "Saturday Night Live"
for how long?

00:01:11.471 --> 00:01:14.240 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I've -- probably about
six or seven years

00:01:14.240 --> 00:01:15.842 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think I held that job.
-Amazing!

00:01:15.842 --> 00:01:19.712 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, what I said in the book,
did you recognize it

00:01:19.712 --> 00:01:21.281 align:start size:94% position:6%
or do you have
a different process?

00:01:21.281 --> 00:01:24.818
-Well, I mean, the one thing
I want to talk to you most about

00:01:24.818 --> 00:01:26.886 align:start size:94% position:6%
is collaboration.
-Ah.

00:01:26.886 --> 00:01:29.556 size:78% position:39%
-Because you sort of
speak a lot about how

00:01:29.556 --> 00:01:34.761 align:start size:94% position:6%
collaboration brought out
the best in your creativity.

00:01:34.761 --> 00:01:35.628 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yes, I think so.

00:01:35.628 --> 00:01:38.031 align:start size:94% position:6%
If I always wrote with
Graham Chapman.

00:01:38.031 --> 00:01:39.899 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I felt if I was writin
with Graham,

00:01:39.899 --> 00:01:44.871
I would usually get somewher
that I wouldn't get on my own,

00:01:44.871 --> 00:01:50.777
even if it was a result of
a set of misunderstandings

00:01:50.777 --> 00:01:52.045 line:92%
-You know, I was wondering -

00:01:52.045 --> 00:01:54.380 align:start size:94% position:6%
you know, because one of the
things I should point out

00:01:54.380 --> 00:01:57.517 align:start size:94% position:6%
about this book
is you believe that people

00:01:57.517 --> 00:01:59.052 align:start size:94% position:6%
do have a creativity
unlocked in them.

00:01:59.052 --> 00:02:02.288
Because I think a lot of peopl
might just think to themselves

00:02:02.288 --> 00:02:03.623 line:92%
"I'm not a creative person."

00:02:03.623 --> 00:02:05.391
And one of the reasons
you point out in the book

00:02:05.391 --> 00:02:08.194 align:start size:94% position:6%
is that creativity
is not ever really taught

00:02:08.194 --> 00:02:10.130 align:start size:94% position:6%
in schools as a skill.
-No!

00:02:10.130 --> 00:02:12.165 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It's not allowed
to develop early on.

00:02:12.165 --> 00:02:14.834 size:84% position:42%
-It's kind of amazing
that you can go through

00:02:14.834 --> 00:02:18.238 align:start size:94% position:6%
a whole good
educational career

00:02:18.238 --> 00:02:21.641 align:start size:94% position:6%
without anyone ever telling yo
about creativity.

00:02:21.641 --> 00:02:22.842 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
It's astounding.

00:02:22.842 --> 00:02:24.077 align:start size:94% position:6%
But that's just the way
we think.

00:02:24.077 --> 00:02:26.746 align:start size:94% position:6%
And we accept it without reall
questioning it.

00:02:26.746 --> 00:02:32.085
I mean, I had no idea that I had
any creative ability at al

00:02:32.085 --> 00:02:34.387 align:start size:94% position:6%
because I got into Cambridge
on science.

00:02:34.387 --> 00:02:37.190 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it's quite hard
to be creative

00:02:37.190 --> 00:02:39.259 line:92%
if you're studying science

00:02:39.259 --> 00:02:41.594 align:start size:94% position:6%
unless you're Stephen Hawking,
you know?

00:02:41.594 --> 00:02:44.297 size:78% position:39%
-Yeah, you never want
to hear that you have

00:02:44.297 --> 00:02:46.533 line:92%
a very creative scientist.

00:02:46.533 --> 00:02:48.535 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:48.535 --> 00:02:49.769 line:92%
Although, I guess we can tak

00:02:49.769 --> 00:02:51.437 align:start size:94% position:6%
some creative scientists
right now.

00:02:51.437 --> 00:02:52.238 size:78% position:39% line:92%
I shouldn't say that.

00:02:52.238 --> 00:02:53.973 align:start size:94% position:6%
But let me ask this,
when did you --

00:02:53.973 --> 00:02:56.209 align:start size:94% position:6%
because it was sort of later -
not later,

00:02:56.209 --> 00:02:58.411 align:start size:94% position:6%
but you weren't
in your adolescence

00:02:58.411 --> 00:03:02.448
when you realized that you
wanted to be a comedian.

00:03:02.448 --> 00:03:06.519 align:start size:94% position:6%
What was the first time like
that you wrote comedy?

00:03:06.519 --> 00:03:09.622 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Um, I wrote some sketches
at Cambridge.

00:03:09.622 --> 00:03:12.692 size:88% position:44%
I mean, I did one or two
"house entertainments,"

00:03:12.692 --> 00:03:13.860 line:92%
they were called at school

00:03:13.860 --> 00:03:16.462 align:start size:94% position:6%
but it never occurred to m
I might finish up.

00:03:16.462 --> 00:03:18.498 align:start size:94% position:6%
I came from the lower
middle class,

00:03:18.498 --> 00:03:21.201 align:start size:94% position:6%
and everybody was either
a solicitor,

00:03:21.201 --> 00:03:23.603 size:88% position:44%
which is a lawyer that
doesn't appear in court,

00:03:23.603 --> 00:03:27.407
or they became an accountant
or they ran a shop, you know

00:03:27.407 --> 00:03:28.741 line:92%
If you're Weston-super-Mare,

00:03:28.741 --> 00:03:29.943 align:start size:94% position:6%
you're not going
to be a comedian

00:03:29.943 --> 00:03:33.379 align:start size:94% position:6%
any more than you're
going to be a matador or,

00:03:33.379 --> 00:03:34.981 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
you know, a pope.

00:03:34.981 --> 00:03:37.584 align:start size:94% position:6%
It just isn't
on the radar screen.

00:03:37.584 --> 00:03:40.453 align:start size:94% position:6%
But when I discovered I coul
make people laugh,

00:03:40.453 --> 00:03:42.889 size:81% position:41%
I never thought I'd go
into the profession.

00:03:42.889 --> 00:03:46.292 align:start size:94% position:6%
But what's so lovely about
making people laugh

00:03:46.292 --> 00:03:47.694 line:92%
is that it's a good feeling.

00:03:47.694 --> 00:03:52.165
It's a good feeling for you an
a good feeling for them, right

00:03:52.165 --> 00:03:53.566 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And did you --
the first time --

00:03:53.566 --> 00:03:56.269
because I certainly remember
those early times of havin

00:03:56.269 --> 00:03:59.305
that rush of not just feelin
good because they're laughing,

00:03:59.305 --> 00:04:01.441 align:start size:94% position:6%
but knowing that they were
feeling good as well.

00:04:01.441 --> 00:04:04.544 align:start size:94% position:6%
Was that an immediate opiate
for you,

00:04:04.544 --> 00:04:07.180
the idea of making people laugh?
-Yes. Yes.

00:04:07.180 --> 00:04:07.914 size:81% position:41% line:92%
It's a lovely feeling.

00:04:07.914 --> 00:04:11.251 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, and I still get it
I went out on the stage

00:04:11.251 --> 00:04:15.955 align:start size:94% position:6%
at the Acropolis in Athens
last November.

00:04:15.955 --> 00:04:19.425 size:84% position:42%
There were 4,000 people
stacked up on a stage

00:04:19.425 --> 00:04:23.062
that people have been performing
on for 2,000 years.

00:04:23.062 --> 00:04:25.098 align:start size:94% position:6%
And there's something abou
being on a stage

00:04:25.098 --> 00:04:27.867 size:84% position:42%
in front of an audience
or going out, you know,

00:04:27.867 --> 00:04:30.003 align:start size:94% position:6%
and doing the opening
monologue.

00:04:30.003 --> 00:04:33.806 align:start size:94% position:6%
It can be scary,
but it's so real.

00:04:33.806 --> 00:04:36.909 align:start size:94% position:6%
There you are trying to make
people laugh.

00:04:36.909 --> 00:04:39.679
-I think the Acropolis --
you definitely have to be

00:04:39.679 --> 00:04:42.749 align:start size:94% position:6%
an icon to play the Acropolis.
-[ Laughs ]

00:04:42.749 --> 00:04:44.751 align:start size:94% position:6%
-They don't --
-I'll have a word

00:04:44.751 --> 00:04:46.185 align:start size:94% position:6%
with the House of Commons
this year

00:04:46.185 --> 00:04:47.687 align:start size:94% position:6%
if I can get you promoted.
-Not a lot of --

00:04:47.687 --> 00:04:50.490 align:start size:94% position:6%
not a lot of open mic nights
at the Acropolis.

00:04:50.490 --> 00:04:53.459 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:53.459 --> 00:04:54.193 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-That's funny.

00:04:54.193 --> 00:04:55.828 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, listen, when you
read the book,

00:04:55.828 --> 00:04:58.364 align:start size:94% position:6%
did you agree with
what I was saying?

00:04:58.364 --> 00:04:59.966 align:start size:94% position:6%
Or do you find
that there were bits

00:04:59.966 --> 00:05:02.368 align:start size:94% position:6%
that were not what
your process was?

00:05:02.368 --> 00:05:04.003 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, one thing
I really agreed with,

00:05:04.003 --> 00:05:06.005 align:start size:94% position:6%
it's I think very hard
to explain.

00:05:06.005 --> 00:05:08.441 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I do want to talk to you
about the fact

00:05:08.441 --> 00:05:10.576 align:start size:94% position:6%
that you have spent
a lot of time studying

00:05:10.576 --> 00:05:11.544 size:84% position:42% line:92%
the human mind as well,

00:05:11.544 --> 00:05:16.949 align:start size:94% position:6%
is the very fact that we can b
creative unconsciously.

00:05:16.949 --> 00:05:17.850 align:start size:94% position:6%
And --
-Yes.

00:05:17.850 --> 00:05:20.553 size:75% position:38%
-'Cause I think that
sometimes, you know,

00:05:20.553 --> 00:05:25.425 align:start size:94% position:6%
when comedy comes out good
it looks as though

00:05:25.425 --> 00:05:27.860 align:start size:94% position:6%
the mind had always
constructed it that way.

00:05:27.860 --> 00:05:30.496
But you talk about the idea that
sometimes you'd hit problems

00:05:30.496 --> 00:05:32.265 align:start size:94% position:6%
and all that it would take
to solve it

00:05:32.265 --> 00:05:34.867 line:92%
would be a good night's sleep.

00:05:34.867 --> 00:05:36.102 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
And I couldn't figure out

00:05:36.102 --> 00:05:41.574
why a problem that I was unabl
to sort out at 10:00 at night,

00:05:41.574 --> 00:05:43.343 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I could wake up
the next morning,

00:05:43.343 --> 00:05:45.778 align:start size:94% position:6%
make a cup of coffee
and sit down,

00:05:45.778 --> 00:05:46.679 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
and the solution,

00:05:46.679 --> 00:05:48.981 align:start size:94% position:6%
in 90 seconds
I could see what to do,

00:05:48.981 --> 00:05:51.117 size:75% position:38%
and I couldn't think
what was the problem

00:05:51.117 --> 00:05:52.552 size:78% position:39% line:92%
the previous evening.

00:05:52.552 --> 00:05:56.889 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I realized it was only
because my unconscious

00:05:56.889 --> 00:06:01.661 align:start size:94% position:6%
was actually -- went on workin
while I was asleep.

00:06:01.661 --> 00:06:04.163
And then I lost a script
I was writing with Graham,

00:06:04.163 --> 00:06:05.832 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I knew he'd be
cross with me.

00:06:05.832 --> 00:06:09.669 align:start size:94% position:6%
So I had to rewrite it out
by memory

00:06:09.669 --> 00:06:11.070 line:92%
to pretend I hadn't lost it.

00:06:11.070 --> 00:06:12.839 line:92%
And then I found the original,

00:06:12.839 --> 00:06:15.875 size:84% position:42%
and the one I had done
from memory was better.

00:06:15.875 --> 00:06:19.278 align:start size:94% position:6%
It was more concise
and clever and tight.

00:06:19.278 --> 00:06:20.580 line:92%
It was a better bit of writing

00:06:20.580 --> 00:06:23.916 align:start size:94% position:6%
But I hadn't been trying
to make it better.

